# _redirects — Cloudflare Pages
#
# Cloudflare Pages only understands `[source] [destination] [status]`. The
# status is optional and defaults to 302, and Cloudflare documents that
# rewrites using non-redirect statuses such as 404 are unsupported:
#   https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# So the old bare-status lines (`/internal/* 404`, `/*.php 404`, …) never
# blocked anything — `404` was parsed as the destination and the rule was
# dropped. A production probe confirmed it: /test-results/.last-run.json
# returned 200. Real 404s for internal, excluded and attack paths are now
# returned by the Pages Function in functions/_middleware.js, which is the
# mechanism Cloudflare recommends for returning a status `_redirects` cannot.
# On Vercel those paths are simply absent from the built dist/ tree.
#
# Only genuine redirects belong in this file.

# Legacy MeishiBridge support URL.
/meishibridge /meishi-scanner/ 301
/meishibridge/ /meishi-scanner/ 301
